Subject: VMS: add mch_calc_cell_size()

term.c's update_cell_size() calls mch_calc_cell_size() when FEAT_EVAL or
FEAT_IMAGE is defined (added with image popups, PR #20136). os_unix.c defines
it inside its #ifndef VMS block, next to the TIOCGWINSZ code VMS does not
have, and os_vms.c has no version, so VIM.EXE fails to link on VMS:
%ILINK-W-USEUNDEF, undefined symbol MCH_CALC_CELL_SIZE. Add one to os_vms.c
that reports the cell size as unknown, as os_unix.c does when the ioctl fails.

--- a/src/os_vms.c
+++ b/src/os_vms.c
@@ -219,6 +219,20 @@
     screen_start();
 }
 
+# if defined(FEAT_EVAL) || defined(FEAT_IMAGE)
+/*
+ * Try to get the current terminal cell size.  The VMS terminal driver knows
+ * the size in characters only, so report it as unknown (-1 x -1); the caller
+ * then uses 8 x 16.
+ */
+    void
+mch_calc_cell_size(struct cellsize *cs_out)
+{
+    cs_out->cs_xpixel = -1;
+    cs_out->cs_ypixel = -1;
+}
+# endif
+
     char_u *
 mch_getenv(char_u *lognam)
 {
